                    "action_type": "MODIFY_TOOL_CODE",
                    "action_details": {
                        "module_path": "agent_tools.scheduling_tools",
                        "function_name": "set_reminder",
                        "suggested_code_change": "import datetime\n\ndef set_reminder(task_description: str, time_string: str):\n    try:\n        # Attempt to parse the time string using multiple formats\n        for fmt in ('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S', '%H:%M', '%I:%M %p', '%I:%M%p', '%I %p', '%I%p'):\n            try:\n                reminder_time = datetime.datetime.strptime(time_string, fmt).time()\n                break  # Exit the loop if parsing succeeds\n            except ValueError:\n                pass  # Continue to the next format if parsing fails\n        else:\n            # If none of the formats work, attempt relative time parsing\n            try:\n                minutes_from_now = int(time_string.split(' ')[1])\n                reminder_time = (datetime.datetime.now() + datetime.timedelta(minutes=minutes_from_now)).time()\n            except (ValueError, IndexError):\n                return 'Error: Invalid time format. Please use a valid time format like HH:MM or specify minutes from now (e.g., in 15 minutes).'\n\n        # Get today's date\n        today = datetime.date.today()\n\n        # Combine today's date with the reminder time to create a datetime object\n        reminder_datetime = datetime.datetime.combine(today, reminder_time)\n\n        # If the reminder time is in the past, set it for tomorrow\n        if reminder_datetime < datetime.datetime.now():\n            reminder_datetime += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n\n        # Schedule the reminder (implementation details omitted for brevity)\n        print(f'Reminder set for {reminder_datetime}: {task_description}')\n        return f'Reminder set for {reminder_datetime}: {task_description}'\n\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f'An unexpected error occurred: {str(e)}'",
                        "original_code_snippet": "# Original potentially unsafe code (no error handling and time parsing)",
                        "suggested_change_description": "Implemented robust time parsing with multiple formats and relative time handling. Added extensive error handling to catch invalid time formats and other potential issues. The function now returns informative error messages to the user."
                    }
                },
                {
                    "suggestion_id": "SUG_003",
                    "suggestion_text": "Address the 'ToolExecutionError' by implementing a centralized tool invocation and argument validation mechanism. This mechanism should ensure that the correct number and types of arguments are passed to each tool. This could involve creating a wrapper function for each tool that performs argument validation before invoking the tool's underlying code.",
                    "addresses_patterns": [
                        "COMMON_ERROR_TYPE: ToolExecutionError"
                    ],
                    "priority": "High",
                    "action_type": "MODIFY_TOOL_CODE",
                    "action_details": {
                        "module_path": "core.action_executor",
                        "function_name": "execute_tool",
                        "suggested_code_change": "def execute_tool(tool_name: str, **kwargs):\n    try:\n        tool_function = get_tool_function(tool_name)\n        tool_signature = inspect.signature(tool_function)\n        bound_arguments = tool_signature.bind(**kwargs)\n        bound_arguments.apply_defaults()\n\n        # Argument Validation (Example)\n        for name, value in bound_arguments.arguments.items():\n            parameter = tool_signature.parameters[name]\n            if parameter.annotation != inspect.Parameter.empty and not isinstance(value, parameter.annotation):\n                raise TypeError(f'Argument {name} must be of type {parameter.annotation}')\n\n        result = tool_function(**bound_arguments.arguments)\n        return result\n    except TypeError as e:\n        return f'Error: Incorrect argument types or number of arguments for {tool_name}. Details: {e}'\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f'Error executing {tool_name}: {e}'",
                        "original_code_snippet": "# Original execution with no validation",
                        "suggested_change_description": "Added argument validation based on function signature to prevent ToolExecutionErrors due to incorrect argument types or number of arguments."
                    }
                }
            ],
            "model_used": "gemini-2.0-flash-exp"
        }
    },
